---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Packages
description: Every package on Hex built with Pooka, newest first.
permalink: /packages/
scripts: [packages]
---
{%- set count = packages.list.length %}
<section class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Packages</span>
      <h1>The <em>burrow</em> of packages.</h1>
      <p><strong class="total" data-total>{{ count if packages.reachable else "All" }}</strong> <span data-total-noun>{{ "package" if count == 1 else "packages" }}</span> on <a href="https://hex.pm">Hex</a> built with Pooka. Erlang and Gleam packages work too: add them with <code>pooka add</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="mascot" src="/assets/mascots/mascot-curious.png" alt="" width="200">
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight" data-packages>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="package-list" data-list>
      {%- for p in packages.list %}
      {% include "partials/package-row.njk" %}
      {%- else %}
      <div class="empty"><img src="/assets/mascots/mascot-curious.png" alt=""><p>Browse <a href="https://hex.pm/packages?search=build_tool%3Apooka">Pooka packages on hex.pm</a>.</p></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="notice" style="margin-top:48px">
      <img src="/assets/mascots/mascot-waving.png" alt="">
      <div>
        <h3>Publish yours</h3>
        <p>Packages published with <code>pooka publish</code> appear here automatically. The <a href="/docs/publishing/">publishing guide</a> walks through it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
